BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-future-leaders-bitsummit-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART:20261105T053000Z
DTEND:20261105T060000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 AEDT: Screen Australia Future Leaders Delegation: Bi
 tSummit 2027 (Kyoto)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 05 Nov 2026 at 17:00 AEDT.\n\nScreen Australia's Future 
 Leaders Delegation sends up to eight early-to-mid career Australian gamema
 kers to BitSummit 2027 in Kyoto\, Japan (21-23 May 2027)\, one of Asia's l
 eading independent games festivals.\n\nOrganisation: Screen Australia\nLoc
 ation: Delegation to BitSummit 2027 in Kyoto\, Japan (21-23 May 2027)\, wi
 th a pre-departure workshop in Melbourne. Open to Australian citizens or p
 ermanent residents\, or incorporated Australian companies.\nAward: AUD 6\,
 000 per delegate towards flights\, accommodation\, event tickets\, ground 
 transportation and meals\, plus covered travel costs for the pre-departure
  workshop and the opportunity to exhibit a game on the Australia stand. Up
  to eight delegates.\nDuration: BitSummit runs 21-23 May 2027 in Kyoto\; m
 andatory pre-departure workshop in Melbourne in mid-April 2027\n\nMore: ht
 tps://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/future-leaders-delegation-bitsummit-
 2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/future-leaders-delegation-bitsu
 mmit-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Delegation to BitSummit 2027 in Kyoto\, Japan (21-23 May 2027)\, w
 ith a pre-departure workshop in Melbourne. Open to Australian citizens or 
 permanent residents\, or incorporated Australian companies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:processing-foundation-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Processing Foundation Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Processing Foundation's 2027 fellowship cycle supports arti
 sts\, educators and creative technologists working on open-source projects
 \, with a USD 10\,000 stipend over an 8-month fellowship period.\n\nOrgani
 sation: Processing Foundation\nLocation: USA only. The Collective Intellig
 ence track is remote (US-based)\; Gaming the System is hybrid in Los Angel
 es\; DIY Computing is hybrid in New York City.\nAward: USD 10\,000 stipend
  over the 8-month fellowship\, plus open-source software mentorship\, coho
 rt collaboration\, professional development and public presentation opport
 unities. No application fee.\nDuration: Approximately 8 months\, 25 Januar
 y to 26 September 2027.\n\nMore: https://processingfoundation.org/programs
 /fellowships/fellowship-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://processingfoundation.org/programs/fellowships/fellowship-2027/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:USA only. The Collective Intelligence track is remote (US-based)\;
  Gaming the System is hybrid in Los Angeles\; DIY Computing is hybrid in N
 ew York City.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-europe-media-video-games-immersive-content-2027@artificialnouv
 eau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART:20270202T153000Z
DTEND:20270202T160000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 CET: Creative Europe MEDIA: European Video Games and
  Immersive Content Development 2027 (up to EUR 200\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 02 Feb 2027 at 17:00 CET.\n\nThe MEDIA strand's annual d
 evelopment scheme for video games and immersive content (call CREA-MEDIA-2
 027-DEVVGIM) funds the pre-production of interactive narrative works with 
 original content and quality gameplay intended for commercial release on P
 C\, console\, mobile or XR platforms.\n\nOrganisation: Creative Europe MED
 IA (European Commission / EACEA)\nLocation: EU Member States\, EEA and cou
 ntries associated to Creative Europe MEDIA. For game and XR production com
 panies established and majority-owned in a MEDIA country.\nAward: Lump-sum
  grant of up to EUR 200\,000 per project\, set at 60 percent of the estima
 ted budget. Total call budget EUR 13\,500\,000. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Development from concept to first playable prototype (first playable\
 , vertical slice\, alpha\, demo). Call opened 30 September 2026.\n\nMore: 
 https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/oppo
 rtunities/topic-details/CREA-MEDIA-2027-DEVVGIM?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/o
 pportunities/topic-details/CREA-MEDIA-2027-DEVVGIM?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:EU Member States\, EEA and countries associated to Creative Europe
  MEDIA. For game and XR production companies established and majority-owne
 d in a MEDIA country.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-emerging-gamemakers-fund-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270225
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270226
SUMMARY:Deadline: Screen Australia: Emerging Gamemakers Fund (round closing
  25 February 2027\, up to AUD 30\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Screen Australia's Emerging Gamemakers Fund backs early-career 
 Australian game makers with small grants to build a prototype or to finish
  and release a micro-scale original game.\n\nOrganisation: Screen Australi
 a\nLocation: Australia. Individuals must be Australian citizens or permane
 nt residents\; companies must be incorporated and run from Australia. ABN 
 required.\nAward: Up to AUD 30\,000 per project. No application fee.\nDura
 tion: Prototype creation or completion and release of a micro-scale game w
 ith a total budget of up to AUD 500\,000. Round opens 14 December 2026\; o
 utcomes about 12 weeks after the deadline.\n\nMore: https://www.screenaust
 ralia.gov.au/fund/emerging-gamemakers-fund-2/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/emerging-gamemakers-fund-2/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia. Individuals must be Australian citizens or permanent re
 sidents\; companies must be incorporated and run from Australia. ABN requi
 red.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-games-production-fund-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270225
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270226
SUMMARY:Deadline: Screen Australia: Games Production Fund (round closing 25
  February 2027\, up to AUD 100\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Screen Australia's Games Production Fund supports Australian in
 dependent studios whose game already has an early-stage prototype and need
 s funding to reach a significant development milestone: completion or rele
 ase\, Early Access\, a demo\, a vertical slice or an accolade-ready protot
 ype.\n\nOrganisation: Screen Australia\nLocation: Australia. Incorporated 
 companies carrying on business in Australia with central management and co
 ntrol in Australia\; sole traders\, trusts and public companies are not el
 igible.\nAward: Up to AUD 100\,000 per project. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Takes an original Australian independent game with an existing early 
 prototype to a significant milestone (completion\, release\, Early Access\
 , demo\, vertical slice or accolade-ready prototype). Round opens 14 Decem
 ber 2026.\n\nMore: https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/games-productio
 n-fund/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/games-production-fund/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia. Incorporated companies carrying on business in Australi
 a with central management and control in Australia\; sole traders\, trusts
  and public companies are not eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:zoud-gamelab-finlit-game-jam-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Zoud GameLab 2026: Global Game Jam financial-literacy jam
  (prize and funding pool up to USD 140\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Zoud GameLab is a month-long virtual game jam run by Global Gam
 e Jam and Zoud\, the UAE's national financial wellbeing initiative\, under
  the theme Make FinLit Fun. Participants build a game that integrates fina
 ncial literacy in a meaningful way\; this is part of the judging criteria\
 , and a scoring rubric is published on the jam page.\n\nOrganisation: Zoud
  (UAE National Financial Wellbeing and Sustainability Initiative) with Glo
 bal Game Jam\nLocation: Online\, worldwide. Open to participants aged 18 a
 nd over in any country\; solo developers\, teams of any size and studios.\
 nAward: Shared prize and development-support funding pool of up to USD 140
 \,000 across best overall game\, runner-up\, third place\, financial-liter
 acy impact\, regional perspective\, compelling gameplay and a Best Game fr
 om the UAE award\; individual prize amounts are not published. No entry fe
 e.\nDuration: Month-long online jam\, 15 October to 15 November 2026\; win
 ners announced December 2026.\n\nMore: https://itch.io/jam/zoud-gamelab?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://itch.io/jam/zoud-gamelab?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, worldwide. Open to participants aged 18 and over in any c
 ountry\; solo developers\, teams of any size and studios.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:playful-obscura-arthouse-games-residency-africa-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Playful Obscura 2027: Arthouse Games Residency Africa (Ad
 dis Ababa\, Goethe-Institut and A MAZE.)
DESCRIPTION:Playful Obscura is the Goethe-Institut's arthouse games residen
 cy for Africa\, co-run with the Berlin playful-media festival A MAZE. Afte
 r editions in Ho (2025) and Accra (2026)\, the third edition moves to Addi
 s Ababa with Creative HUB Ethiopia\, the British Council and Alliance Ethi
 o-Francaise.\n\nOrganisation: Goethe-Institut Addis Abeba\, with Creative 
 HUB Ethiopia\, A MAZE.\, British Council and Alliance Ethio-Francaise\nLoc
 ation: Addis Ababa\, Ethiopia. For artists and game developers based in Af
 rica working in playful media and arthouse games.\nAward: Three-week funde
 d residency hosting two artists at a time. 2027 financial terms were not p
 ublished in the call excerpt we could verify\; the 2026 Accra edition prov
 ided accommodation\, a production budget of up to EUR 1\,000 and a EUR 300
  stipend. No application fee.\nDuration: Residency 25 January to 14 Februa
 ry 2027 in Addis Ababa\; open call 16 October to 1 November 2026\, with an
  online Q&A on 22 October.\n\nMore: https://www.goethe.de/ins/za/en/kul/mu
 t/p27.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.goethe.de/ins/za/en/kul/mut/p27.html?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Addis Ababa\, Ethiopia. For artists and game developers based in A
 frica working in playful media and arthouse games.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:big-festival-gamescom-latam-2027-indie-submissions@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART:20270116T022900Z
DTEND:20270116T025900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 21:59 EST: BIG Festival at gamescom latam 2027: free indie
  game submissions (Sao Paulo\, awards with cash prizes)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 15 Jan 2027 at 21:59 EST.\n\nBIG Festival\, the indie ga
 mes competition inside gamescom latam in Sao Paulo\, has opened free submi
 ssions for its 2027 edition. The 2026 edition drew a record 966 submission
 s from 75 countries.\n\nOrganisation: gamescom latam / BIG Festival\nLocat
 ion: Sao Paulo\, Brazil (Distrito Anhembi). Open to independent developers
  anywhere in the world.\nAward: Free submission and a no-cost exhibition s
 lot for selected games\, plus eligibility for the BIG Festival awards. 202
 7 prize amounts are not yet published\; in 2025 Best Game carried BRL 5\,0
 00 and in 2026 the WINGS Award carried EUR 2\,000 in cash.\nDuration: Subm
 issions 16 October 2026 to 15 January 2027\; festival 22 to 25 April 2027.
 \n\nMore: https://latam.gamescom.global/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://latam.gamescom.global/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sao Paulo\, Brazil (Distrito Anhembi). Open to independent develop
 ers anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:realities-in-transition-rit2-oc3-uncharted-grounds-lev-2027@artificialn
 ouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART:20261106T222900Z
DTEND:20261106T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Realities in Transition RiT2 Open Call #3: Unch
 arted Grounds\, a VRChat world residency with L.E.V. Festival (EUR 10\,000
  fee plus up to EUR 15\,000 production)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 06 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nRealities in Transition (Ri
 T2)\, a Creative Europe XR cooperation project\, and host partner L.E.V. F
 estival invite artists with VR development experience to co-create a walka
 ble VRChat world conceived as a voyage\, with 5 to 7 environments\, 3 to 5
  avatars and optional NPC players\; events\, social worlds and theatre pie
 ces are not wanted.\n\nOrganisation: Realities in Transition (RiT2\, Creat
 ive Europe)\, with L.E.V. Festival\nLocation: Online residency\, with a Te
 st Lab at L.E.V. Gijon and a premiere at L.E.V. Matadero (Madrid)\, Spain.
  Check the RiT residencies page for country eligibility.\nAward: EUR 10\,0
 00 gross artist fee per selected artist (paid in three instalments) plus u
 p to EUR 15\,000 gross production budget shared among the team. No travel 
 or accommodation included. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: 6 mont
 hs online\, January to June 2027\; Test Lab in May 2027\, final presentati
 on in September 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.realities-in-transition.eu/rit-
 2-open-call-3/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.realities-in-transition.eu/rit-2-open-call-3/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online residency\, with a Test Lab at L.E.V. Gijon and a premiere 
 at L.E.V. Matadero (Madrid)\, Spain. Check the RiT residencies page for co
 untry eligibility.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
